<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd"\>
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Eigenframe is not sandboxed and cannot be. It reads the Space list through
      private CGS window server calls and installs a session event tap, and
      neither is available to a sandboxed process. That makes the hardened
      runtime the only thing standing between this app's Input Monitoring grant
      and any other process running as the same user, so the build script signs
      with the hardened runtime option enabled.

      Do NOT add any of these three entitlements. Each one re-opens that path:
        com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
        com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
        com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory

      Note for future edits: XML forbids a doubled hyphen inside a comment, and
      AMFI rejects the whole file when it sees one. Spell out command line flags
      in prose here rather than writing them literally.

      The key below is a sandbox entitlement and is inert for an unsandboxed
      app. The Input Monitoring prompt is actually driven by the
      CGEvent.tapCreate call plus NSInputMonitoringUsageDescription in
      Info.plist. It is kept so the declared intent shows up in the output of
      codesign when displaying entitlements.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.input-monitoring</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
